From d75b7c18ab17f09db86139459de7560ae44706a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Braden <snufflyb14@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:57:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ppu: lifted guest stores take an inline fast path
 (vm_store_span, spu_coh_bitmap)

Loads already inline; stores were still a call into the loader's vm_write*, which checks the null page,
bounds, the debug watches and raw-SPU registers, then calls spu_coh_is_reserved out of line. On a render-bound
UE3 screen those two were 33% of the render thread's CPU. The lifter's header now does the common case
inline (address in [0x10000, vm_store_span), no SPU reservation on the line, byte-swap, write) and falls back
to the out-of-line store otherwise. vm_store_span is armed by the first out-of-line store (ppu_vm_size is set
by then) and stays 0 while PPU_WVAL/PPU_WWATCH/PS3_NULL_SWEEP are set. PPU_NO_INLINE_STORES opts out.
